WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:07.010
Pom Klementieff had to undergo a major transformation
in order to portray the empath Mantis in the

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.020
MCU and it wasn't just a physical one.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.840
Her character has such a unique background
and power-set that Klementieff had to go through

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.140
some serious mental effort to become the adorable
alien we know and love.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.100
Actors who portray superheroes tend to have
some pretty strict dietary rules in order

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:28.360
to achieve the impressive physique they need
that is even more apparent when you factor

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.860
in the ridiculous body standards that celebrity
women must deal with.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:36.740
But Klementieff's diet is not as strict as
you might think she just changes it to suit

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.320
her needs for whatever role she is currently
playing.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.680
In an interview with Byrdie, Klementieff discussed
her upbringing and how her diet changes depending

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.420
on the current role she is playing.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.000
She explained:

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.820
"I grew up eating amazing homemade French
food.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.020
Now if I tell myself I can't eat something,
I'm just going to be obsessed with it.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:54.600
Like bread.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.520
I love bread… for me, it's about quantity.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:58.340
Balance.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.020
I eat a little bit of everything….

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.620
I'm vegan in L.A., but not in Europe."

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.800
Pom Klementieff's first major Hollywood role
was in Spike Lee's remake of Oldboy.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.880
She told Filler that she actually came prepared
to show off her fighting skills during the

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.940
audition for that film, and that she enjoyed
her boxing and Tae Kwon Do training so much

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.820
that she continued after filming wrapped.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:24.399
It's easy to assume that may have had something
to do with her getting cast in the action-heavy

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.700
world of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:32.240
Superhero Jacked writes that Klementieff does
almost no "traditional" workouts it's all

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.960
practical stunt and fight training.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.360
This also helps prepare her for the rigors
of long shooting days.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.200
She told Filler:

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.100
"I had to train three hours a day for two
months.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.360
You are sore everyday, and you're working
on your soreness!"

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:49.280
Mantis isn't the heaviest hitter in the Guardians
of the Galaxy or Avengers films, but maybe

00:01:49.289 --> 00:01:53.780
Klementieff's training in fighting and stunts
will open her character up to some more action-heavy

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.000
roles in future MCU films.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.920
Several stars of the Guardians of the Galaxy
films need to spend hours in the makeup chair

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.500
to achieve their alien looks.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:09.300
Karen Gillan knows it's not easy being blue,
Dave Bautista's Drax is encased in prosthetics

00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:13.230
and intricate tattoos, and don't even get
us started on how much fur they have to glue

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.220
on Bradley Cooper.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.940
"HAH HAH HAH HAH HAH HAH HAH."

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:18.060
"That's a fake laugh."

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.140
"It's real!"

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.460
Klementieff's Mantis is no exception, but
she actually does not require quite as much

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.800
time in the makeup chair as some of her costars.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.580
Klementieff typically spends about two-and-a-half
to three hours in makeup to play Mantis.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:36.319
That might sound crazy, but it's only about
half the time that Zoe Saldana has to spend

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.220
getting painted green to play Gamora.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:42.780
That's because of the combination of practical
makeup effects and CGI that brings Mantis

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:48.450
to life her look is created with a few basic
prosthetics and, according to Metro, quote,

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.140
a "lot of beauty makeup."

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.940
Apparently, one of the most difficult makeup
challenges Klemtieff faces is keeping a straight

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:55.440
face.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.220
She said of costar Chris Pratt,

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.480
"It's hard to keep a straight face around
him.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:04.340
I laughed so hard I was crying, and my makeup
artist was kind of mad at me."

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.610
Part of the struggle in making an audience
care about alien characters is to make them

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.180
just human enough to be relatable.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:12.560
"I am Mantis."

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:17.640
"What are you doing?"

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:19.200
"Smiling."

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.400
Klementieff has recognized the difficulty
and experimentation that went into making

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:29.079
sure Mantis was slightly off-putting but still
someone you could empathize with and cheer

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:29.580
for.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.460
She told Metro:

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:35.340
"We tried a lot of stuff, we tried different
wigs; at some point the makeup artists drew

00:03:35.349 --> 00:03:40.620
veins on my face; contact lenses; at some
point I looked really crazy and then we decided

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.129
to go for something a little more human black
eyes that make me look like a bug but at the

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:47.160
same time something you can still connect
to."

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.780
It was extremely important to get Mantis'
eyes just right.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.240
People are able to learn a great deal about
another's emotions and mental state by looking

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.200
in their eyes.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.900
Despite going way out into left field for
their initial shots at Mantis' makeup, the

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.900
team eventually anchored her humanity through
her eyes.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:10.220
Mantis has a very fascinating superpower one
that could be difficult to portray on screen.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.950
Her ability to feel and manipulate the emotions
of others is pretty passive compared to her

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.180
butt-kicking companions.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.840
But sadly, Klementieff is able to draw on
several experiences from her real life in

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.880
order to bring genuine pain and emotion to
her character.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:28.460
Her father died when she was only five years
old, while her mother was mentally ill and

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:29.980
unable to care for her alone.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.840
She went on to live with her aunt and uncle
not long after her father's death.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.400
The uncle who was caring for her died on her
18th birthday, and her brother took his own

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.080
life on her 25th birthday.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.780
She told the Philadelphia Inquirer that acting
has helped her deal with the pain.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.760
"It's life and s---- could be worse.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.280
It's cathartic in a way.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.180
Sometimes you relive things and it helps you
to deal with it.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.460
You relive it and become accepting of it and
you touch other people's hearts with your

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:56.900
experience and performance.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:57.800
It's beautiful!"

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:02.620
She was able to channel some of the loneliness
and abandonment she felt as a child into how

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:06.560
her long-isolated and empathetic character
would view the world around her.

